<title>FRENCH GUIANA: Ariane rocket to launch PanAmSat satellite.</title>
<headline>Ariane rocket to launch PanAmSat satellite.</headline>
<dateline>CAYENNE, French Guiana 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Europe's 98th Ariane rocket is scheduled to blast off from French Guiana early on Friday carrying a communications satellite for PanAmSat, the Arianespace company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The PanAmSat-6 (PAS-6) satellite will provide direct television broadcast services to South America for the Connecticut-based global satellite operator.</p>
<p>The 3.4-tonne satellite, built in the United States by Space Systems/Loral, will be carried by an Ariane 44P rocket equipped with four solid strap-on boosters.</p>
